# Post-Phase Documentation Closeout

Run this checklist **only after** the active plan phase is fully implemented: required code is done, tests and acceptance checks pass, evidence is captured, and the phase is ready to hand off. Do **not** run mid-implementation or while work is still in progress.

## When to trigger

- The current `docs/plans/<phase>/` step is implemented and finalized.
- The user indicates the phase is complete, or all items in `tests-and-acceptance.md` are satisfied.
- Run as the **last step** of the session — after code, tests, and the completion report.

## 1. Analyze session context

From the conversation and change set, extract:

- New or changed product/architecture decisions
- Spike outcomes that resolved open questions
- Deviations from the phase spec (with rationale)
- Stable contracts, APIs, commands, fixtures, feature flags, and known limitations
- Docs listed under the phase README **Documentation output** section

## 2. Update `docs/decisions-log.md`

Append a dated entry:

- Phase ID and title (e.g. `Phase 01 — Plugin Kernel`)
- Decisions made or confirmed
- Spike resolutions
- Explicit deferrals with target phase
- References to new or updated ADRs

If a decision changes authoritative product behavior, also update `docs/00-product-charter-and-decisions.md` and add or amend an ADR under `docs/architecture/adr/`.

## 3. Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md`

Add under `[Unreleased]` (or a dated section when releasing):

- Phase number and name
- User-visible and developer-facing changes
- Breaking changes, migrations, and new commands
- Paths to test/evidence artifacts (not binary blobs)

## 4. Update other documentation as needed

Update only what the session actually changed:

| Trigger | Target |
|---|---|
| Resolved or new open spike | `docs/11-open-decisions.md` |
| API/schema/contract change | `docs/03-data-model-rest-api.md`, Bruno/OpenAPI notes |
| Architecture boundary change | Relevant spec under `docs/02-enterprise-architecture.md`, integration guides |
| New ADR-worthy choice | `docs/architecture/adr/ADR-NNN-*.md` |
| Pinned version/license change | Source lock and integration docs cited by the phase |
| Handoff differs from plan | Phase folder README or technical-spec |

When any doc conflicts with `docs/00-product-charter-and-decisions.md`, fix the doc in the same change set.

## 5. Manifest and closeout

- If files were added, removed, or renamed under `docs/`, update `docs/MANIFEST.md` when maintained.
- End with a closeout summary: phase complete (yes/no), docs updated (list paths), remaining risks for the next phase.

Do not commit unless the user asks. Do not edit unrelated documentation.
